==English==

===Etymology===
{{uder|en|la|studiōsus}}. First recorded in English circa 1350.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-studious.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstuːdi.əs/|/ˈstjuːdi.əs/}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːdiəs|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Given to [[thought]], or to the examination of subjects by contemplation; [[contemplative]].
# Dedicated to [[study]]; devoted to the acquisition of knowledge from books
#: {{usex|en|a '''studious''' scholar}}
# {{lb|en|usually followed by an infinitive or by "of"}} Earnest in endeavors; [[attentive]]; diligent
#: {{usex|en|be '''studious''' to please}}
#: {{usex|en|She is '''studious''' to find new friends and allies}}
# Planned with study; deliberate; studied.
# Favorable to study; suitable for thought and contemplation
#: {{usex|en|the '''studious''' shade}}

====Antonyms====
